If the spin alone is retained and the detector is ignored, its reduced state is $\rho_{\mathrm{spin}}
=|\alpha|^2\ket{u}\bra{u}
+|\beta|^2\ket{d}\bra{d},$ assuming orthogonal pointer records. The interference terms have disappeared from the local description because they are stored in correlations with the apparatus.

